{"name":"Blue Bird Day","hex":"#237fac","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"bird","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An animal of the clade (traditionally class) Aves in the phylum Chordata, characterized by being warm-blooded, having feathers and wings usually capable of flight, having a beaked mouth, and laying eggs.","Any winged animal."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To observe or identify wild birds in their natural environment.","To catch or shoot birds; to hunt birds."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bird"},{"term":"day","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-5 language code for Land Dayak languages."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is above the horizon and it lights the sky.","A period of time equal or almost equal to a full day-night cycle, being 24 hours long."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/day"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bird Day","blocks":[{"text":"Bird Day or World Migratory Bird Day is the name of several holidays celebrating birds. Various countries observe such a holiday on various dates."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bird_Day","wikidata":"Q1161367"},{"title":"Bluebird","blocks":[{"text":"The bluebirds are a North American group of medium-sized, mostly insectivorous or omnivorous passerine birds in the genus Sialia of the thrush family (Turdidae)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Eastern_Bluebird%2C_crop.jpg/330px-Eastern_Bluebird%2C_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluebird","wikidata":"Q853286"},{"title":"Bird","blocks":[{"text":"Birds are vertebrate animals constituting the class Aves, characterised by feathers, toothless beaked jaws, the laying of hard-shelled eggs, a high metabolic rate, a four-chambered heart, and a strong yet lightweight skeleton. They are warm-blooded, live worldwide, and range in size from the 5.5 cm (2.2 in) bee hummingbird to the 2.8 m common ostrich. There are over 11,000 living species of birds, classified in 44 orders. More than half of the world's bird species are passerine or \"perching\" birds. Nearly all birds have wings whose development varies according to the life style of each species. Wings, which are modified forelimbs, gave birds the ability to fly, although further evolution has led to the loss of flight in some birds, including ratites, penguins, and diverse endemic island species. The only known groups without wings are the extinct moa and elephant birds. Birds are the only extant members of Dinosauria, and are a type of paravian theropods. The digestive and respiratory systems of birds are uniquely adapted for flight. Some bird species of aquatic environments, particularly seabirds and some waterbirds, have further evolved for swimming. The study of birds is called ornithology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Kleiber_Flug.jpg/330px-Kleiber_Flug.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bird","wikidata":"Q5113"},{"title":"Day","blocks":[{"text":"A day is the time period of a full rotation of the Earth with respect to the Sun. On average, this is 24 hours. As a day passes at a given location it experiences morning, afternoon, evening, and night. This daily cycle drives circadian rhythms in many organisms, which are vital to many life processes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Day","wikidata":"Q573"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/2e/IMBD_Theme_Art_2014.jpg/250px-IMBD_Theme_Art_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2e/IMBD_Theme_Art_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/2e/IMBD_Theme_Art_2014.jpg/250px-IMBD_Theme_Art_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"International Migratory Bird Day poster 2014","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIMBD_Theme_Art_2014.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/2016-IMBD-Eng-Poster-Web.jpg/500px-2016-IMBD-Eng-Poster-Web.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/2016-IMBD-Eng-Poster-Web.jpg/500px-2016-IMBD-Eng-Poster-Web.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"International Migratory Bird Day 2016 poster by Lionel Worrell","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2016-IMBD-Eng-Poster-Web.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Bird_watching_at_Landsort%2C_April_2009-2.jpg/500px-Bird_watching_at_Landsort%2C_April_2009-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Bird_watching_at_Landsort%2C_April_2009-2.jpg/500px-Bird_watching_at_Landsort%2C_April_2009-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bird watching at Landsort, April 2009","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABird_watching_at_Landsort%2C_April_2009-2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Mountain_Bluebird.jpg/500px-Mountain_Bluebird.jpg?utm_source=en.w